==Problem==

Let <imath>ABCDEF</imath> be a regular hexagon with side length <imath>1</imath>. Denote by <imath>X</imath>, <imath>Y</imath>, and <imath>Z</imath> the midpoints of sides <imath>\overline {AB}</imath>, <imath>\overline{CD}</imath>, and <imath>\overline{EF}</imath>, respectively. What is the area of the convex hexagon whose interior is the intersection of the interiors of <imath>\triangle ACE</imath> and <imath>\triangle XYZ</imath>?

<imath>\textbf{(A)}\ \frac {3}{8}\sqrt{3} \qquad \textbf{(B)}\ \frac {7}{16}\sqrt{3} \qquad \textbf{(C)}\ \frac {15}{32}\sqrt{3} \qquad  \textbf{(D)}\ \frac {1}{2}\sqrt{3} \qquad \textbf{(E)}\ \frac {9}{16}\sqrt{3}</imath>

